      <p>Travelling solo, as a couple or with a few friends? A <strong>joining group safari</strong> is a practical way to see Tanzania’s wildlife without paying for a private vehicle. You travel with other visitors, share the safari transport and guiding service, and enjoy a chance to meet people who are just as excited about the adventure as you are.</p>
      <p>At <strong>Deep Tanzania Tours</strong>, we arrange shared safaris to Tarangire National Park, Ngorongoro Crater, Serengeti National Park and Lake Manyara. You can choose from short one-day trips or longer journeys of up to six days. The itineraries below use budget camping and, where the route requires it, budget lodge accommodation around Karatu.</p>
      <div class="dtt-jg-advice"><p><strong>Good to know before you join:</strong> All our joining group safaris begin and end in Arusha. Hotels before or after the safari and airport transfers are not included, but we can arrange them at an additional cost. If you would like different accommodation or a more flexible itinerary, ask about a private safari.</p></div>
